{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 699fa6d5e8111aa1767146a09995213cd394e68e, on planner/actenv-amend5-20261116, its one artifact `notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md`, for request 362e5841 under my promise e547957b. This verdict names the one implementation: the fifth amendment (request f9b404f9, promise 9a576b69). Main 7a6fcadf is the parent, and the diff is that one file, 117 lines added and 3 removed. The head lands after the LS-5 and LC-4 head.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- Section 5.7. No placement outside the scope holds a grant, so a local instance and the agent host state `standing` as null, and an exploration that reaches the grant check answers `authority-unavailable`. The table row of the agent host drops \"the grants that it holds for its key\". The two open questions match ruling d038a2ee: a value check shared with `judgeGrant` and a body grant with no freshness proof, which change `packages/derive`, and the choice between a membership replica and the standing that `issueSession` reads.\n- Section 6. The context reader at the constructor and its first adapter, the replica alone with `standing` null, match rulings 16211297 and 13bbb177. An `unavailable` exploration stops no submit.\n- Section 6.1. The rule that a `ref` is a value, and each of its bullets and its stated limit, match ruling 4dffc26a.\n- Section 15. The corrected row gives the three results of a stop, as ruling 9930cf7f gives them: nothing written, a version with no mark from a `source` preview, or a version and its mark after one call of the signer for the signer stop, the store stop, and `full` with `bytes` after the build. The new row lists the ten stops and the four reasons of `full`, as ruling 850da1af confirms. That ruling supersedes the nine rows of 22ae2bd0. The paragraphs on the two size checks of custody, on `source` and on `versions-full` match 9930cf7f and 850da1af.\n- Section 19. The six rows cite the rulings above and name the right sections. The opening paragraph adds section 5 and the open question.\n\nWhat I checked against source at 7a6fcadf:\n\n1. `packages/scope/src/authority.ts:538` says that no presented grant is read.\n2. `packages/derive/src/judge.ts` refuses `revision-moved` at line 400 and runs the grant check at lines 427 to 447. With `grants` null, line 446 answers `authority-unavailable`. The guards come after, as check 10.\n3. `judgeGrant` takes an `ObservationUse` at `packages/derive/src/grant.ts:305`.\n4. `issueSession` calls `standingOf` at `packages/scope/src/sessions.ts:389`. `SESSION_SECONDS` is 600, so \"up to 600 seconds old\" holds.\n5. `packages/client/src/custody.ts:567` checks the caller's estimate before the build, and line 577 checks the built record after `build()`, which signs.\n\nCheap checks: `check-notes.mjs 7a6fcadf 699fa6d5` reports 0 warnings, `check-doc-links.mjs` exits 0, the commit-message check passes with 1 checked and 0 flagged, and `git diff --check` is clean. Under the notes-only ruling, I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The amendment records the planner's C4 rulings where the note's sections already place them. It states the gap of E2 and E3 as open and blocks both steps on the owner's answer, instead of naming a source that the code does not have. The port and its one adapter keep the seam that a later adapter of standing would use.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. An instance presents no guessed grant, and `predictionGrant` stays inside the prediction of the member's own pending acts. The scope keeps reading standing itself. One fact for the owner's decision: a standing carried in the session answer is unchecked by any journal and up to 600 seconds old, so an exploration under it can report an act as permitted after a revocation. The scope still refuses that act, so the error stays in the exploration. Answer (e) of d038a2ee owes what a reader checks on that value.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The corrected row of section 15 replaces a sentence that was too narrow with the three actual results.\n\nQualifications that stand: this is a design note, and C4 has not built the context reader, the `ref` rule or the ten stops. The test that pins the order of the basis check and the grant check is owed by C4. The standing question waits for the owner. This approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing, after the LS-5 and LC-4 head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8073dddc9d49a5f7b87d6125080329150fd23283","binding":"assigned","head":"699fa6d5e8111aa1767146a09995213cd394e68e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e547957bcc5e348373e5a4ba48999f6c097882e5\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9a576b6923b83b02d6729ecfa129221f9b766763\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e547957bcc5e348373e5a4ba48999f6c097882e5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}